[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 821,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 764,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128022,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 356,
        "headingId": 764,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Pseudomyogenic haemangioendothelioma is a rarely metastasizing endothelial neoplasm that often presents as multiple nodules in different tissue planes and histologically mimics a myoid tumour or epithelioid sarcoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T12:12:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 822,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 765,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128023,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 356,
        "headingId": 765,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>9138/1 Pseudomyogenic haemangioendothelioma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T12:12:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 823,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 766,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128024,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 356,
        "headingId": 766,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2E81.OZ &amp; XH26F6 Neoplastic haemangioma, unspecified &amp; Pseudomyogenic (epithelioid sarcoma&ndash;like) haemangioendothelioma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T12:12:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 824,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 767,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128025,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 356,
        "headingId": 767,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> epithelioid sarcoma&ndash;like haemangioendothelioma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T12:12:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 825,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 768,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128026,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 356,
        "headingId": 768,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T12:12:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 826,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 769,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128027,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 356,
        "headingId": 769,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Pseudomyogenic haemangioendothelioma most commonly involves the lower extremities (55%); the upper extremities and trunk are less commonly affected (20% each), and the head and neck are rarely involved (5%) {12502927; 1371711; 23381465; 21263239}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T12:12:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 827,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 770,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128028,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 356,
        "headingId": 770,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients present with painless or painful nodules; ulceration may be present. In about 60% of cases the disease is multifocal, involving multiple tissue planes, most commonly the skin and subcutis, but it may also involve skeletal muscle and bone {12502927; 21263239; 1371711; 23381465}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T12:12:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 828,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 771,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128029,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 356,
        "headingId": 771,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Young men (mean age: 30&nbsp;years) are most commonly affected (M:F&nbsp;ratio: 3.5:1) {21263239}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T12:12:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 829,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 772,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128030,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 356,
        "headingId": 772,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T12:12:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 830,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 773,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128031,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 356,
        "headingId": 773,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Pseudomyogenic haemangioendothelioma has rearrangements of <em>FOSB</em>, including <em>SERPINE1</em>::<em>FOSB</em>, <em>ACTB</em>::<em>FOSB</em>, <em>WWTR1</em>::<em>FOSB</em>, <em>CLTC</em>::<em>FOSB</em>, and <em>EGFL7</em>::<em>FOSB</em> {24374978; 30459475; 30256258; 31243110; 32749039; 33550637}. This results in upregulation, with FOSB acting as an active transcription factor capable of its own regulation {24374978; 29511030}. Tumours with <em>ACTB</em>::<em>FOSB</em> fusions are more likely to be solitary {30256258}. Tumours with <em>EGFL7</em>::<em>FOSB</em> may be more aggressive {33550637}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T12:12:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 837,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 780,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128032,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 356,
        "headingId": 780,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Grossly, the tumour is poorly defined, with a grey to white firm cut surface. Most are &lt;&nbsp;30&nbsp;mm in size {21263239}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T12:12:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 831,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 774,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128033,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 356,
        "headingId": 774,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Pseudomyogenic haemangioendotheliomas are variably composed of infiltrative sheets and fascicles of spindled (most commonly) to epithelioid cells with dense, eosinophilic cytoplasm {21263239; 12502927}. Atypia is usually mild, and tumour nuclei are vesicular with small nucleoli. Significant nuclear atypia may be seen in about 10% of cases {21263239}. Admixed neutrophils are seen in approximately 50%.</p>\r\n<p>By immunohistochemistry, they are positive for keratins (most often with AE1/AE3 clones, less often MNF116), FLI1, ERG, and FOSB, but negative for CD34 {21263239; 12502927; 27515856; 28009608}. About 50% are positive for CD31, and focal expression of SMAs is seen in as many as one&nbsp;third of cases. SMARCB1 expression is retained {21263239}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T12:12:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 832,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 775,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128034,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 356,
        "headingId": 775,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T12:12:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 833,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 776,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128035,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 356,
        "headingId": 776,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Detection of <em>FOSB</em> rearrangement may be helpful.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T12:12:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 836,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 779,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128036,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 356,
        "headingId": 779,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> fascicles or sheets of spindled to epithelioid cells with dense eosinophilic cytoplasm, vesicular nuclei, and expression of ERG and AE1/AE3.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> demonstration of FOSB expression or <em>FOSB</em> rearrangement.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T12:12:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 834,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 777,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128037,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 356,
        "headingId": 777,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T12:12:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 835,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 778,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128038,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 356,
        "headingId": 778,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Local recurrence or development of new nodules in the same region is frequent (~60%) {21263239}. Lymph node and distant metastases are uncommon (&lt;&nbsp;5%) {21263239}. Histopathological features are not predictive.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T12:12:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]